{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"install-apps","name":"Install apps","version":"1.0.0","apiVersion":1,"author":"zabique","description":"Install .wgt and .tpk packages from the dashboard, signed with your own developer certificate, with a Home tile like a store app. No internet access.","permissions":["exec"],"main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Install apps"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Install apps\n\nA Vetro Shard: install `.wgt` and `.tpk` packages on the TV from the dashboard (**Vetro Shards → Install apps**).\n\n- **Upload and install** a package of up to 400 MB, as it is or signed first with your developer certificate.\n- After a web app (`.wgt`) is installed it gets a row in Samsung's app registry and a tile on the Samsung Home\n  row, like a store app, and the Vetro launcher is asked to read its list again.\n- **Installed apps**: launch, add to Home, uninstall (the registry row and the Home tile go with it). Firmware\n  packages are listed on request but never uninstalled from here.\n\nIt talks to nothing outside the TV.\n\n## Your developer certificate\n\nSigning needs the author and distributor `.p12` files of a Tizen certificate profile made for your TV, and\ntheir passwords. You give them once, under **Developer certificate**:\n\n- the files are converted to PEM on the TV with its own `openssl`, and the result is kept in this Shard's\n  `config.json` on the TV (mode 600). That file holds your **private keys**: anyone with root on the TV can read\n  it, as they can read everything else there;\n- the passwords are used for the conversion and not kept;\n- nothing is sent back to the page except the certificate's subject and expiry date;\n- **Remove from the TV** deletes them. Removing the Shard deletes them too.\n\nNo certificate ships with the Shard.\n\n## The `exec` permission: commands it runs\n\nAll as root, through `ctx.execute`, and only when you press something on the page (opening the page lists the\ninstalled apps).\n\n| When | Command |\n| --- | --- |\n| the page opens, Refresh | `pkgcmd -l`, `app_launcher -l` |\n| Save certificate | `openssl pkcs12 -in <file> -nokeys` and `-nocerts -nodes` in a private `mktemp` folder under `/tmp`, removed when the command ends; the password reaches openssl on stdin, never on a command line; `openssl x509 -noout -subject -enddate` |\n| Upload and install | `pkgcmd -i -t wgt|tpk -p /tmp/install-apps-shard/<file>`: only a file this Shard uploaded, with a name of letters, digits, dot, dash and underscore |\n| after a `.wgt` install, Add to Home | `registry.js`: reads `/opt/dbspace/.pkgmgr_parser.db`, adds one row to `/opt/dbspace/.webappservice.db` (a copy of the database is kept first as `/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vetro-webappservice.db.bak`), copies the app's icon, restarts `org.tizen.webappservice`. `home-order.js`: closes Samsung Home if it runs and adds the tile to its row file, as one transaction with a rollback |\n| Launch | `app_launcher -s <app id>` |\n| Uninstall | `pkgcmd -u -n <package id>`, then the registry row and the Home tile are removed the same way |\n\nPackage and app ids must match `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]` before they reach a command.\n\nOne request goes to Vetro itself: `POST http://127.0.0.1:8099/dock {\"action\":\"refresh\"}`, so the launcher shows\na new or removed app at once. If that fails nothing else is affected.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.js`: routes, upload, certificate, install and uninstall.\n- `sign.js`: the package signer (author-signature.xml and signature1.xml, SHA-512 digests, RSA-SHA512), using\n  only Node's own modules. Its output was compared byte for byte with the `tizen` npm package's signer on a\n  test key.\n- `registry.js`, `home-order.js`: copies of `app/service/webapp-registry.js` and `app/service/home-order.js`\n  from the same repository. A Shard cannot use Vetro's modules, so it carries them.\n- `page.html`: the page.\n\n## Limits\n\n- **Tested on one TV only: a QN85A (Tizen 6).** The registry and Home row steps depend on Samsung's files as\n  they are on that firmware; on another model an install may succeed and the tile not appear.\n- Needs the root helper, `openssl`, `sqlite3` and `pkgcmd` on the TV.\n- Zip64 packages and encrypted zips are not signed. A `.tpk` is signed the same way as a `.wgt`; that was\n  not tried on a TV.\n- The registry step applies to web apps only.\n","home-order.js":"// Copy of app/service/home-order.js from zabique/vetro (branch extras-050), unchanged below this line: a Shard\n// cannot reach Vetro's own modules, so it carries what it needs. Only add() and prune() are used here.\n'use strict';\n\n// Home app order: the ordered list stored in the CoBA \".appLayerCache\" file\n// under the csfs data dir (or the home.media one on TVs with the new Home). Each line is a section item:\n//   s/livetv@<source>        live TV source (TV Plus, RF, ...)\n//   d/webapp@<packageId|storeId>  web application\n// The file shape is: <version>\\n<entries...>\\nEOFC OBA\\n (some firmwares: EOFCOBA). The Home reads it to\n// order the app row; reordering = rewriting the entries. A backup is kept and\n// restore() puts it back. Applying a change needs the Home/CoBA host to reload.\n\nvar BASE = '/opt/usr/home/owner/apps_rw/com.samsung.tv.csfs/data';\nvar BASE_NEW_HOME = '/opt/usr/home/owner/apps_rw/com.samsung.tv.home.media/data';\n// Shell prelude: D is the first data dir that holds a cache file, the csfs one when neither does.\nvar PICK_DIR = 'D=' + BASE + '\\nfor c in ' + BASE + ' ' + BASE_NEW_HOME + '; do if [ -f \"$c/.appLayerCache.1\" ] || [ -f \"$c/.appLayerCache.2\" ]; then D=$c; break; fi; done\\n';\nvar FILES = ['.appLayerCache.1', '.appLayerCache.2'];\nvar TERM = 'EOFC OBA';\n// Some firmwares (e.g. T-PTMDDEUC-1400.1) write the terminator without the space.\nvar TERMS = ['EOFC OBA', 'EOFCOBA'];\nvar MAX = 300;\n// Type part: letters, digits, \"_\" and \".\" (physical inputs use e.g. \"source.layer.hdmi\"). The \"@id\" part\n// is absent on some source layers (QN85A, T-NKM2DEUC: \"s/source.layer.remoteworkspace\").\nvar ENTRY = /^[sd]\\/[A-Za-z0-9_.]+(?:@[^\\s]+)?$/;\n\nvar CLOSE_HOME = 'if app_launcher -r com.samsung.tv.csfs 2>/dev/null | grep -q \"result: running\"; then app_launcher -k com.samsung.tv.csfs >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; fi\\n';\n\nfunction wrap(script) { return 'echo ' + Buffer.from(script).toString('base64') + ' | base64 -d | sh'; }\nfunction check(r) { if (r.exit_code || r.timed_out) throw Error(r.stderr || r.stdout || 'Home order unavailable'); return r.stdout || ''; }\n\nfunction parse(text) {\n    var lines = String(text || '').replace(/\\r/g, '').split('\\n');\n    if (lines.length < 3) throw Error('Unrecognized Home order');\n    var end = lines.findIndex(function (l) { return TERMS.indexOf(l.trim()) >= 0; });\n    if (end < 0) throw Error('Home order terminator missing');\n    var version = lines[0].trim();\n    if (!/^\\d+$/.test(version)) throw Error('Unrecognized Home order version');\n    var entries = lines.slice(1, end).map(function (l) { return l.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n    if (entries.length > MAX) throw Error('Too many Home order entries');\n    validate(entries);\n    return { version: version, entries: entries, term: lines[end].trim() };\n}\n\nfunction validate(entries) {\n    if (!Array.isArray(entries) || entries.length > MAX) throw Error('Invalid order');\n    entries.forEach(function (e) { if (!ENTRY.test(e)) throw Error('Invalid Home order entry: ' + e); });\n}\n\nfunction render(order) {\n    validate(order.entries);\n    return order.version + '\\n' + order.entries.join('\\n') + '\\n' + (TERMS.indexOf(order.term) >= 0 ? order.term : TERM) + '\\n';\n}\n\nfunction sameSet(a, b) {\n    if (a.length !== b.length) return false;\n    var x = a.slice().sort().join('\\n'), y = b.slice().sort().join('\\n');\n    return x === y;\n}\n\nfunction Order(execute) { this.execute = execute; this.busy = false; }\n\nOrder.prototype.read = function () {\n    var script = PICK_DIR + 'cat \"$D/' + FILES[0] + '\" 2>/dev/null || cat \"$D/' + FILES[1] + '\" 2>/dev/null';\n    return this.execute(wrap(script), 8000).then(function (r) {\n        var order = parse(check(r));\n        order.file = null; // Fallback read does not identify the selected cache.\n        return order;\n    });\n};\n\n// entries must be a permutation of the current ones (reorder only, no add/remove).\nOrder.prototype.write = function (entries) {\n    return this.commit(function (cur) {\n        validate(entries);\n        if (!sameSet(cur.entries, entries)) throw Error('Entries must be unchanged, only reordered');\n        return entries;\n    });\n};\n\n// Store apps appear in the row by store id (digits); webapps.txt maps each store id to the package and app ids\n// that belong to it. Returns {storeId: [ids]}.\nfunction parseWebapps(text) {\n    var map = {}, cur = null;\n    String(text || '').replace(/\\r/g, '').split('\\n').forEach(function (l) {\n        l = l.trim();\n        if (/^\\d{8,}$/.test(l)) { cur = l; map[cur] = []; }\n        else if (cur && l && TERMS.indexOf(l) < 0 && /^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(l)) map[cur].push(l);\n    });\n    return map;\n}\n\n// Installed package ids: names of the app folders and the package manager's lists.\nfunction parseInstalled(text) {\n    var set = {};\n    String(text || '').replace(/\\r/g, '').split('\\n').forEach(function (l) {\n        var m = /pkgid \\[([^\\]]+)\\]/.exec(l);\n        if (m) set[m[1]] = true;\n        else if (/^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(l.trim())) set[l.trim()] = true;\n    });\n    return set;\n}\n\n// Row entries whose app is no longer installed. Only web app entries are judged, and only when every id they\n// stand for is known and missing: a store id that webapps.txt does not resolve is kept.\nfunction staleEntries(entries, webapps, installed) {\n    var has = function (id) { return !!installed[id] || !!installed[id.split('.')[0]]; };\n    return entries.filter(function (e) {\n        var m = /^d\\/webapp@([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)$/.exec(e);\n        if (!m) return false;\n        var ids = /^\\d{8,}$/.test(m[1]) ? webapps[m[1]] : [m[1]];\n        return !!ids && ids.length > 0 && !ids.some(has);\n    });\n}\n\n// Samsung Home drops an uninstalled app from its row only if it is running when the package manager says so;\n// the dock closes the Home after every Home press, so it usually is not, and the tile stays. prune() removes\n// those entries. The Home is closed first (when running) so it cannot write its old list back; it reads the\n// file again at its next start.\nOrder.prototype.prune = function () {\n    var removed = [];\n    return this.commit(function (cur, facts) {\n        removed = staleEntries(cur.entries, facts.webapps, facts.installed);\n        return removed.length ? cur.entries.filter(function (e) { return removed.indexOf(e) < 0; }) : null;\n    }, this.facts.bind(this), CLOSE_HOME)\n        .then(function (o) { o.removed = removed; return o; });\n};\n\n// The store mapping and the installed packages, for prune() and add().\nOrder.prototype.facts = function () {\n    var script = PICK_DIR + 'echo \"--cache\"; cat \"$D/' + FILES[0] + '\" 2>/dev/null || cat \"$D/' + FILES[1] + '\" 2>/dev/null\\n' +\n        'echo \"--webapps\"; cat \"$D/webapps.txt.2\" 2>/dev/null || cat \"$D/webapps.txt.1\" 2>/dev/null\\n' +\n        'echo \"--installed\"; ls /opt/usr/apps /opt/usr/globalapps /usr/apps /usr/globalapps 2>/dev/null; pkgcmd -l 2>/dev/null; pkgcmd -l --global 2>/dev/null; true';\n    return this.execute(wrap(script), 20000).then(function (r) {\n        var out = check(r), w = out.indexOf('--webapps\\n'), i = out.indexOf('--installed\\n');\n        if (w < 0 || i < 0) throw Error('Home apps unavailable');\n        var installed = parseInstalled(out.slice(i));\n        // Never judge from a list that failed to load: the package manager knows hundreds of packages.\n        if (Object.keys(installed).length < 20) throw Error('Installed package list unavailable; nothing changed');\n        return { webapps: parseWebapps(out.slice(w, i)), installed: installed };\n    });\n};\n\n// Samsung Home's \"Add to Home\": puts an installed web app on the row as d/webapp@<package id>, at index (default:\n// the end). Nothing changes when the app is already there, under its package id or its store id. The Home is\n// closed first, as for prune().\nOrder.prototype.add = function (packageId, index) {\n    if (typeof packageId !== 'string' || !/^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}$/.test(packageId)) return Promise.reject(Error('Invalid package id'));\n    var entry = 'd/webapp@' + packageId, added = null;\n    return this.commit(function (cur, facts) {\n        var stores = Object.keys(facts.webapps).filter(function (s) {\n            return facts.webapps[s].some(function (id) { return id === packageId || id.split('.')[0] === packageId; });\n        });\n        if (cur.entries.indexOf(entry) >= 0 || stores.some(function (s) { return cur.entries.indexOf('d/webapp@' + s) >= 0; })) return null;\n        if (!facts.installed[packageId]) throw Error(packageId + ' is not installed');\n        var at = typeof index === 'number' && index >= 0 && index <= cur.entries.length ? Math.floor(index) : cur.entries.length;\n        var next = cur.entries.slice();\n        next.splice(at, 0, entry);\n        added = entry;\n        return next;\n    }, this.facts.bind(this), CLOSE_HOME).then(function (o) { o.added = added; return o; });\n};\n\n// Read the row, let change() compute the new entry list (null: nothing to do), write both caches as one\n// transaction and confirm by reading back. facts() gathers extra input first; before runs ahead of the write.\nOrder.prototype.commit = function (change, facts, before) {\n    var self = this;\n    if (this.busy) return Promise.reject(Error('Home order change already in progress'));\n    this.busy = true;\n    return Promise.resolve(facts ? facts() : null).then(function (f) { return self.read().then(function (cur) { return [cur, f]; }); }).then(function (cf) {\n        var cur = cf[0], entries = change(cur, cf[1]);\n        if (!entries) { cur.saved = false; return cur; }\n        validate(entries);\n        var payload = Buffer.from(render({ version: cur.version, entries: entries, term: cur.term })).toString('base64');\n        var script = (before || '') + transactionScript(payload, false);\n        self.transactionStarted = true;\n        return self.execute(wrap(script), 10000).then(function (r) {\n            check(r);\n            return self.read();\n        }).then(function (o) { if (JSON.stringify(o.entries)!==JSON.stringify(entries)) throw Error('Written order not confirmed by readback'); o.saved = true; return o; });\n    }).catch(function (e) {\n        if (!self.transactionStarted) throw e;\n        return self.execute(wrap(rollbackScript()), 10000).then(function (r) { check(r); throw Error(e.message + ' · previous caches restored'); }, function (restoreError) { throw Error(e.message + ' · restore failed: ' + restoreError.message); });\n    }).finally(function () { self.busy = false; self.transactionStarted = false; });\n};\n\nfunction rollbackScript() {\n    return 'set -e\\n' + PICK_DIR + 'for f in ' + FILES.join(' ') + '; do if [ -f \"$D/$f.vetro-txn\" ]; then cp -p \"$D/$f.vetro-txn\" \"$D/$f.vetro-tmp\"; mv -f \"$D/$f.vetro-tmp\" \"$D/$f\"; elif [ -f \"$D/$f.vetro-missing\" ]; then rm -f \"$D/$f\"; fi; done';\n}\nfunction transactionScript(payload, restoring) {\n    var prepare = 'set -e\\n' + PICK_DIR + 'for f in ' + FILES.join(' ') + '; do rm -f \"$D/$f.vetro-txn\" \"$D/$f.vetro-missing\"; if [ -f \"$D/$f\" ]; then cp -p \"$D/$f\" \"$D/$f.vetro-txn\"; [ -f \"$D/$f.vetro-bak\" ] || cp -p \"$D/$f\" \"$D/$f.vetro-bak\"; else touch \"$D/$f.vetro-missing\"; fi; done\\n';\n    if (restoring) prepare += 'for f in ' + FILES.join(' ') + '; do [ -f \"$D/$f.vetro-bak\" ] || { echo \"Backup Home incompleto\" >&2; exit 1; }; done\\n';\n    var fill = restoring ? 'cp -p \"$D/$f.vetro-bak\" \"$D/$f.vetro-tmp\"' : 'if [ -f \"$D/$f\" ]; then cp -p \"$D/$f\" \"$D/$f.vetro-tmp\"; else touch \"$D/$f.vetro-tmp\"; fi; echo ' + payload + ' | base64 -d > \"$D/$f.vetro-tmp\"';\n    return prepare + 'committed=0\\ntrap \\'if [ \"$committed\" != 1 ]; then for f in ' + FILES.join(' ') + '; do if [ -f \"$D/$f.vetro-txn\" ]; then cp -p \"$D/$f.vetro-txn\" \"$D/$f\"; elif [ -f \"$D/$f.vetro-missing\" ]; then rm -f \"$D/$f\"; fi; done; fi\\' EXIT\\nfor f in ' + FILES.join(' ') + '; do ' + fill + '; done\\nfor f in ' + FILES.join(' ') + '; do mv -f \"$D/$f.vetro-tmp\" \"$D/$f\"; done\\ncommitted=1\\necho OK';\n}\nOrder.prototype.restore = function () {\n    var self = this;\n    if (this.busy) return Promise.reject(Error('Home order change already in progress'));\n    this.busy = true;\n    return this.execute(wrap(transactionScript(null, true)), 10000).then(function (r) { check(r); return self.read(); }).finally(function () { self.busy = false; });\n};\n\nmodule.exports = { PICK_DIR: PICK_DIR, BASE_NEW_HOME: BASE_NEW_HOME, staleEntries: staleEntries, parseWebapps: parseWebapps, parseInstalled: parseInstalled, transactionScript: transactionScript, rollbackScript: rollbackScript, Order: Order, parse: parse, render: render, validate: validate, BASE: BASE, FILES: FILES, TERM: TERM };\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Install apps: upload a .wgt or .tpk from the dashboard, sign it with your own developer certificate when\n// asked, install it with pkgcmd, then make it show up the way a store install does: a row in Samsung's web app\n// registry (registry.js) and a tile on the Samsung Home row (home-order.js). Also lists the installed\n// packages, launches and uninstalls them (an uninstall takes the registry row and the Home tile away again).\n//\n// The certificate is yours: two .p12 files and their passwords, given once on the page. The TV's openssl turns\n// them into PEM, which is kept in this Shard's config.json (readable by the service only) and never sent back.\n//\n// Every value that reaches a shell command is checked against a strict pattern first: package and app ids are\n// [A-Za-z0-9_.-], and only files this Shard wrote under its upload folder can be installed.\n// Needs `exec`: openssl, pkgcmd, app_launcher and the registry and Home row changes all run as root.\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var fs = require('fs'), path = require('path'), http = require('http'), crypto = require('crypto');\n    var Registry = require('./registry.js').Registry, Order = require('./home-order.js').Order;\n\n    var DIR = '/tmp/install-apps-shard';\n    var MAX_PACKAGE = 400 * 1024 * 1024;\n    var CHUNK_BODY = 4 * 1024 * 1024;          // one base64 chunk (the page sends 512 KB of file per chunk)\n    var SMALL_BODY = 256 * 1024;\n    var PACKAGE_ID = /^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}$/;\n    var APP_ID = /^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,128}$/;\n    var FILE = /^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,120}\\.(wgt|tpk)$/;\n    var BASE64 = /^[A-Za-z0-9+\\/=\\s]{1,90000}$/;\n    var VETRO_PORT = 8099;                       // Vetro's own port, for the launcher refresh below\n\n    var page = '', uploads = {}, busy = false, registry = null, homeOrder = null;\n\n    function buffer(text, encoding) { return typeof Buffer.alloc === 'function' ? Buffer.from(text, encoding) : new Buffer(text, encoding); }\n    function wrap(script) { return 'echo ' + buffer(script, 'utf8').toString('base64') + ' | base64 -d | sh'; }\n    function problem(message, code, step) { var e = new Error(message); e.statusCode = code; e.step = step || null; return e; }\n    function json(res, body, code) {\n        if (res.headersSent) return;\n        res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n    }\n    function failure(res) {\n        return function (e) { json(res, { ok: false, step: e.step || null, error: String(e && e.message || e) }, e.statusCode || (e.step ? 500 : 503)); };\n    }\n    function readBody(req, limit, done) {\n        var parts = [], size = 0, over = false;\n        req.on('data', function (c) { if (over) return; size += c.length; if (size > limit) { over = true; return done(null); } parts.push(c); });\n        req.on('end', function () {\n            if (over) return;\n            var parsed = null;\n            try { parsed = JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(parts).toString('utf8')); } catch (e) { parsed = null; }\n            done(parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' ? parsed : null);\n        });\n    }\n\n    // ── the developer certificate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // One .p12 to PEM, as root with the TV's openssl. The password goes in through stdin, never on a command\n    // line; the files live in a private folder for the length of the command.\n    function convertScript(p12, password) {\n        var pass = password === '' ? '-passin pass:' : '-passin stdin < \"$T/pw\"';\n        return [\n            'T=$(mktemp -d /tmp/install-apps-cert.XXXXXX) || exit 1',\n            'trap \\'rm -rf \"$T\"\\' EXIT',\n            'chmod 700 \"$T\"',\n            'echo ' + p12 + ' | base64 -d > \"$T/in.p12\"',\n            'echo ' + buffer(password, 'utf8').toString('base64') + ' | base64 -d > \"$T/pw\"',\n            'if ! openssl pkcs12 -in \"$T/in.p12\" -nokeys ' + pass + ' > \"$T/certs.pem\" 2> \"$T/err\"; then echo \"@@ERR\"; cat \"$T/err\"; exit 0; fi',\n            'openssl pkcs12 -in \"$T/in.p12\" -nocerts -nodes ' + pass + ' > \"$T/key.pem\" 2>> \"$T/err\" || { echo \"@@ERR\"; cat \"$T/err\"; exit 0; }',\n            'echo \"@@CERTS\"; cat \"$T/certs.pem\"',\n            'echo \"@@KEY\"; cat \"$T/key.pem\"',\n            'echo \"@@INFO\"; openssl x509 -in \"$T/certs.pem\" -noout -subject -enddate 2>/dev/null',\n            'true'\n        ].join('\\n');\n    }\n    function parseConverted(text) {\n        text = String(text || '');\n        if (text.indexOf('@@ERR') >= 0 || text.indexOf('@@KEY') < 0) {\n            throw problem(/mac verify|invalid password/i.test(text) ? 'Wrong password for this certificate file.' : 'This file could not be read as a .p12 certificate.', 400);\n        }\n        var certs = text.slice(text.indexOf('@@CERTS'), text.indexOf('@@KEY')), rest = text.slice(text.indexOf('@@KEY'));\n        var chain = [], re = /-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----([\\s\\S]*?)-----END CERTIFICATE-----/g, m;\n        while ((m = re.exec(certs))) chain.push(m[1].replace(/\\s+/g, ''));\n        var key = /-----BEGIN (?:RSA )?PRIVATE KEY-----[\\s\\S]*?-----END (?:RSA )?PRIVATE KEY-----/.exec(rest);\n        if (!chain.length || !key) throw problem('The certificate file holds no certificate with its private key.', 400);\n        var info = rest.slice(rest.indexOf('@@INFO'));\n        var subject = /subject\\s*=\\s*(.*)/.exec(info), end = /notAfter\\s*=\\s*(.*)/.exec(info);\n        var out = { chain: chain, key: key[0] + '\\n', subject: subject ? subject[1].trim().slice(0, 200) : '', notAfter: end ? end[1].trim().slice(0, 60) : '' };\n        // The key must be the one of the first certificate.\n        var probe = crypto.createSign('RSA-SHA256').update('install-apps').sign(out.key);\n        // 64 characters a line and no empty line before END (a length that is a multiple of 64 must not leave one).\n        var pem = '-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\\n' + chain[0].match(/.{1,64}/g).join('\\n') + '\\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\\n';\n        if (!crypto.createVerify('RSA-SHA256').update('install-apps').verify(pem, probe)) throw problem('The private key does not belong to the certificate.', 400);\n        return out;\n    }\n    function convert(part, what) {\n        if (!part || typeof part.p12 !== 'string' || !BASE64.test(part.p12)) return Promise.reject(problem('Choose the ' + what + ' .p12 file.', 400));\n        var password = typeof part.password === 'string' ? part.password : '';\n        if (password.length > 256) return Promise.reject(problem('That password is too long.', 400));\n        return ctx.execute(wrap(convertScript(part.p12.replace(/\\s+/g, ''), password)), 20000).then(function (r) {\n            try { return parseConverted(r.stdout); } catch (e) { e.message = what.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + what.slice(1) + ': ' + e.message; throw e; }\n        });\n    }\n    function certs() { var c = ctx.config.get() || {}; return c.certs && c.certs.author && c.certs.author.key ? c.certs : null; }\n    function certSummary() {\n        var c = certs();\n        function one(x) { return x && x.key ? { subject: x.subject || '', notAfter: x.notAfter || '' } : null; }\n        return { author: c ? one(c.author) : null, distributor: c ? one(c.distributor) : null };\n    }\n    function saveCerts(p) {\n        var config = ctx.config.get() || {};\n        if (p.remove === true) { delete config.certs; ctx.config.set(config); return Promise.resolve(certSummary()); }\n        return convert(p.author, 'author').then(function (author) {\n            return (p.distributor && p.distributor.p12 ? convert(p.distributor, 'distributor') : Promise.resolve(null)).then(function (distributor) {\n                config.certs = { author: author };\n                if (distributor) config.certs.distributor = distributor;\n                ctx.config.set(config);\n                return certSummary();\n            });\n        });\n    }\n\n    // ── packages ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // Firmware parts (and Vetro itself) are listed but never uninstalled from here.\n    function systemPackage(id, type) {\n        return type === 'rpm' || id === 'vetrotvapp' || /^(com\\.samsung\\.|org\\.tizen\\.|dtv-|lib-)/.test(id);\n    }\n\n    // pkgcmd -l lines: \"user apps  pkg_type [wgt]  pkgid [X]  name [Y]  version [Z] ...\"; app_launcher -l: \"'name' 'appid'\".\n    function parseApps(text) {\n        var parts = String(text || '').split('===LAUNCHER===');\n        var byPkg = {}, byName = {};\n        String(parts[1] || '').split('\\n').forEach(function (l) {\n            var m = /'([^']+)'\\s+'([^']+)'/.exec(l);\n            if (!m) return;\n            var appId = m[2].trim(), pkg = appId.split('.')[0];\n            byName[m[1].trim()] = appId;\n            if (!byPkg[pkg]) byPkg[pkg] = appId;\n        });\n        var apps = [];\n        String(parts[0] || '').split('\\n').forEach(function (line) {\n            var m = /pkg_type\\s*\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\s*pkgid\\s*\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\s*name\\s*\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\s*version\\s*\\[([^\\]]*)\\]/.exec(line);\n            if (!m) return;\n            var pkgId = m[2], name = m[3] || pkgId;\n            apps.push({\n                name: name, packageId: pkgId, type: m[1], version: m[4] || '',\n                appId: byName[name] && byName[name].split('.')[0] === pkgId ? byName[name] : byPkg[pkgId] || null,\n                // pkgcmd calls everything installed by root \"system apps\", sideloads included: judge by the id.\n                system: systemPackage(pkgId, m[1])\n            });\n        });\n        apps.sort(function (a, b) { return (a.system - b.system) || a.name.localeCompare(b.name); });\n        return apps;\n    }\n\n    // The Vetro launcher lists apps too. A Shard has no handle on it, so Vetro is asked over its own port to\n    // read the list again; if that does not work the launcher simply shows the change later.\n    function refreshLauncher() {\n        try {\n            var body = JSON.stringify({ action: 'refresh' });\n            var req = http.request({ host: '127.0.0.1', port: VETRO_PORT, path: '/dock', method: 'POST',\n                headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'content-length': Buffer.byteLength(body) } }, function (r) { r.resume(); });\n            req.on('error', function () { /* best effort */ });\n            req.setTimeout(8000, function () { req.abort(); });\n            req.end(body);\n        } catch (e) { /* best effort */ }\n    }\n\n    // After an install: Samsung's app registry first (without a row Samsung Home drops the tile), then the Home\n    // row. Never fails the install; each step reports its own result.\n    function show(packageId) {\n        return registry.register(packageId).catch(function (e) { return { registered: false, error: e.message }; }).then(function (reg) {\n            return homeOrder.add(packageId).then(function (o) {\n                if (o.added) refreshLauncher();\n                return { registry: reg, homeRow: { added: o.added } };\n            }).catch(function (e) { return { registry: reg, homeRow: { added: null, error: e.message } }; });\n        });\n    }\n    // After an uninstall: the registry row made here, and the Home tile, go too. Never fails the uninstall.\n    function hide(packageId) {\n        return registry.unregister(packageId).catch(function (e) { return { removed: 0, error: e.message }; }).then(function (reg) {\n            return homeOrder.prune().then(function (o) {\n                if (o.removed.length) refreshLauncher();\n                return { removed: o.removed, registry: reg };\n            }).catch(function (e) { return { removed: [], registry: reg, error: e.message }; });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function apps() {\n        return ctx.execute('pkgcmd -l 2>/dev/null; echo \"===LAUNCHER===\"; app_launcher -l 2>/dev/null', 30000).then(function (r) {\n            return { ok: true, apps: parseApps(r.stdout) };\n        });\n    }\n\n    function upload(p) {\n        var name = String(p.filename || '');\n        if (!FILE.test(name)) throw problem('Choose a .wgt or .tpk file (letters, digits, dot, dash and underscore in its name).', 400);\n        var chunk = Number(p.chunk), total = Number(p.totalChunks);\n        if (!(chunk >= 0 && chunk < total && total <= 4096 && Math.floor(chunk) === chunk)) throw problem('Bad chunk number', 400);\n        if (typeof p.data !== 'string') throw problem('Missing data', 400);\n        var u = uploads[name];\n        if (chunk === 0) u = uploads[name] = { next: 0, size: 0 };\n        if (!u || u.next !== chunk) throw problem('Upload out of order; start again', 409);\n        var buf = buffer(p.data, 'base64');\n        if (u.size + buf.length > MAX_PACKAGE) { delete uploads[name]; throw problem('The package is larger than 400 MB.', 413); }\n        try { fs.mkdirSync(DIR); } catch (e) { if (e.code !== 'EEXIST') throw e; }\n        fs.writeFileSync(path.join(DIR, name), buf, { flag: chunk === 0 ? 'w' : 'a' });\n        u.next++; u.size += buf.length;\n        var done = u.next === total;\n        if (done) delete uploads[name];\n        return { ok: true, chunk: chunk, totalChunks: total, done: done, file: name, size: u.size };\n    }\n\n    function install(p) {\n        var name = String(p.file || ''), file = path.join(DIR, name);\n        if (!FILE.test(name) || !fs.existsSync(file)) return Promise.reject(problem('Upload the package first.', 400));\n        if (busy) return Promise.reject(problem('Another install is running.', 409));\n        var keys = p.sign ? certs() : null;\n        if (p.sign && !keys) return Promise.reject(problem('Add your developer certificate first, or choose \"Install as it is\".', 400, 'sign'));\n        busy = true;\n        function done() { busy = false; fs.unlink(file, function () {}); }\n        var type = /\\.tpk$/.test(name) ? 'tpk' : 'wgt', cmd = 'pkgcmd -i -t ' + type + ' -p ' + file;\n        var signed = !keys ? Promise.resolve(null)\n            : require('./sign.js').signPackage(file, keys).catch(function (e) { e.step = 'sign'; throw e; });\n        var result = signed.then(function (sig) {\n            return ctx.execute(cmd + ' 2>&1', 110000).then(function (r) {\n                var out = r.stdout || '', id = /pkgid\\[([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)\\]/.exec(out);\n                var ok = r.exit_code === 0 && /val\\[ok\\]/.test(out), packageId = id ? id[1] : null;\n                var answer = { ok: ok, signed: !!sig, packageId: packageId, exit_code: r.exit_code,\n                    output: out.split('\\n').filter(function (l) { return !/install_percent/.test(l); }).join('\\n').trim() };\n                if (!ok || !packageId || !PACKAGE_ID.test(packageId)) return answer;\n                return show(packageId).then(function (s) { answer.registry = s.registry; answer.homeRow = s.homeRow; return answer; });\n            });\n        });\n        result.then(done, done);\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    function launch(p) {\n        if (!APP_ID.test(String(p.appId || ''))) return Promise.reject(problem('missing or invalid appId', 400));\n        return ctx.execute('app_launcher -s ' + p.appId + ' 2>&1', 20000).then(function (r) {\n            return { ok: r.exit_code === 0 && !/fail|error/i.test(r.stdout || ''), output: r.stdout };\n        });\n    }\n\n    function uninstall(p) {\n        var id = String(p.packageId || '');\n        if (!PACKAGE_ID.test(id)) return Promise.reject(problem('missing or invalid packageId', 400));\n        if (systemPackage(id)) return Promise.reject(problem('System packages are not uninstalled here.', 403));\n        return ctx.execute('pkgcmd -u -n ' + id + ' 2>&1', 60000).then(function (r) {\n            var ok = r.exit_code === 0 && /val\\[ok\\]/.test(r.stdout || '');\n            return (ok ? hide(id) : Promise.resolve(null)).then(function (home) { return { ok: ok, output: r.stdout, homeRow: home }; });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function register(p) {\n        var id = String(p.packageId || '');\n        if (!PACKAGE_ID.test(id)) return Promise.reject(problem('missing or invalid packageId', 400));\n        return show(id).then(function (s) { return { ok: !!(s.registry && s.registry.registered), registry: s.registry, homeRow: s.homeRow }; });\n    }\n\n    var ACTIONS = { install: install, launch: launch, uninstall: uninstall, register: register, cert: saveCerts };\n\n    return {\n        start: function () {\n            registry = new Registry(ctx.execute);\n            homeOrder = new Order(ctx.execute);\n            page = fs.readFileSync(path.join(ctx.dir, 'page.html'), 'utf8');\n        },\n        stop: function () { uploads = {}; },\n        status: function () { return { certificate: !!certs(), installing: busy }; },\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (req.method === 'GET') {\n                if (sub === 'ui') {\n                    res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n                    res.end(page);\n                    return true;\n                }\n                if (sub === 'apps') { apps().then(function (d) { json(res, d); }, failure(res)); return true; }\n                if (sub === 'cert') { json(res, certSummary()); return true; }\n                return false;\n            }\n            if (req.method !== 'POST') return false;\n            if (sub === 'upload') {\n                readBody(req, CHUNK_BODY, function (p) {\n                    if (!p) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'JSON body expected (up to 4 MB)' }, 400);\n                    try { json(res, upload(p)); } catch (e) { failure(res)(e); }\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(ACTIONS, sub)) return false;\n            readBody(req, SMALL_BODY, function (p) {\n                if (!p) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'JSON body expected' }, 400);\n                var out;\n                try { out = ACTIONS[sub](p); } catch (e) { return failure(res)(e); }\n                out.then(function (d) { json(res, d); }, failure(res));\n            });\n            return true;\n        },\n        // For tests.\n        _internals: { parseApps: parseApps, parseConverted: parseConverted, convertScript: convertScript, DIR: DIR }\n    };\n};\n","page.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"dark light\">\n<title>Install apps</title>\n<style>\n:root{--action:#3b6cf6;--edge:rgba(128,128,128,.4);--danger:#d8443a}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nbody{font:15px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;margin:16px;color:CanvasText;background:Canvas;max-width:980px}\nh2{font-size:17px;margin:0}\n.panel{border:1px solid var(--edge);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;margin:0 0 16px}\n.note{font-size:13px;opacity:.75}\np.note{margin:6px 0 0}\n.row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:center;margin-top:12px}\n.head{justify-content:space-between;margin-top:0}\n.grow{flex:1 1 220px}\nbutton{font:inherit;height:36px;padding:0 14px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--edge);background:transparent;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}\nbutton:hover:not(:disabled){background:rgba(128,128,128,.15)}\nbutton:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}\nbutton:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--action);outline-offset:2px}\nbutton.primary{background:var(--action);border-color:var(--action);color:#fff}\nbutton.primary:hover:not(:disabled){background:var(--action);filter:brightness(1.1)}\nbutton.danger{border-color:var(--danger);color:var(--danger)}\ninput[type=search],input[type=password]{font:inherit;height:36px;width:100%;padding:0 10px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--edge);background:transparent;color:inherit}\nlabel.field{display:grid;gap:4px;font-size:13px}\n.drop{display:grid;gap:4px;justify-items:center;padding:20px 12px;margin:12px 0;border:2px dashed var(--edge);border-radius:10px;text-align:center;cursor:pointer}\n.drop.over{border-color:var(--action)}\n.drop input{max-width:100%}\nfieldset{border:1px solid var(--edge);border-radius:10px;margin:0;padding:10px 12px;display:grid;gap:6px}\nlegend{font-size:13px;padding:0 6px}\nprogress{width:100%;margin-top:12px}\npre{margin:12px 0 0;padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--edge);border-radius:8px;max-height:220px;overflow:auto;font:12px/1.4 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\ndetails>summary{cursor:pointer;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;list-style:none}\ndetails>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}\ndetails>summary::before{content:\"▸\";opacity:.7}\ndetails[open]>summary::before{content:\"▾\"}\n.certs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:12px}\n.pkg-list{display:grid;gap:8px;margin-top:12px}\n.pkg{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--edge);border-radius:10px}\n.pkg-name{font-weight:500}\n.pkg-id{font-size:13px;opacity:.75;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n.tag{font-size:12px;padding:0 5px;border:1px solid var(--edge);border-radius:6px;margin-left:6px;opacity:.75}\n.pkg .row{margin-top:0}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<section class=\"panel\">\n  <h2>Install a package</h2>\n  <p class=\"note\">A .wgt (web app) or .tpk (native app) is uploaded to the TV, signed if you choose so, and installed.\n    The app then gets its tile on the Samsung Home row and in the Vetro launcher, like a store app.</p>\n  <label class=\"drop\" id=\"drop\">\n    <input type=\"file\" id=\"file\" accept=\".wgt,.tpk\">\n    <strong id=\"pick\">Drop a .wgt or .tpk here, or choose a file</strong>\n    <span class=\"note\">Up to 400 MB</span>\n  </label>\n  <fieldset>\n    <legend>Signature</legend>\n    <label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"sign\" value=\"sign\"> Sign with my developer certificate <span class=\"note\" id=\"signNote\"></span></label>\n    <label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"sign\" value=\"asis\" checked> Install as it is <span class=\"note\">the package is already signed for this TV</span></label>\n  </fieldset>\n  <div class=\"row\">\n    <button id=\"go\" class=\"primary\" disabled>Upload and install</button>\n    <span id=\"status\" class=\"note\" aria-live=\"polite\">Choose a package.</span>\n  </div>\n  <progress id=\"progress\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\" hidden></progress>\n  <pre id=\"log\" hidden></pre>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"panel\">\n  <details id=\"certBox\">\n    <summary><h2>Developer certificate</h2><span class=\"note\" id=\"certState\">Checking…</span></summary>\n    <p class=\"note\">The certificate a package is signed with before it is installed: the author and distributor .p12 files\n      of your Tizen certificate profile, made for this TV. They are converted on the TV and kept there, in this\n      Shard's own settings; the passwords are used once and not kept.</p>\n    <div class=\"certs\">\n      <label class=\"field\"><span>Author certificate (.p12)</span><input type=\"file\" id=\"authorFile\" accept=\".p12,.pfx\"></label>\n      <label class=\"field\"><span>Author password</span><input type=\"password\" id=\"authorPw\" autocomplete=\"off\"></label>\n      <label class=\"field\"><span>Distributor certificate (.p12)</span><input type=\"file\" id=\"distFile\" accept=\".p12,.pfx\"></label>\n      <label class=\"field\"><span>Distributor password</span><input type=\"password\" id=\"distPw\" autocomplete=\"off\"></label>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <button id=\"certSave\" class=\"primary\">Save certificate</button>\n      <button id=\"certRemove\" hidden>Remove from the TV</button>\n      <span id=\"certStatus\" class=\"note\" aria-live=\"polite\"></span>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"panel\">\n  <div class=\"row head\"><h2>Installed apps</h2><button id=\"refresh\">Refresh</button></div>\n  <div class=\"row\">\n    <label class=\"field grow\"><span>Filter</span><input id=\"filter\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Name or package id\"></label>\n    <label><input id=\"system\" type=\"checkbox\"> Show system packages</label>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"apps\" class=\"pkg-list\"><p class=\"note\">Reading the installed apps…</p></div>\n</section>\n\n<script>\nfunction $(id){return document.getElementById(id)}\nfunction esc(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[c]})}\nfunction bytes(n){return n<1024?n+' B':n<1048576?(n/1024).toFixed(0)+' KB':(n/1048576).toFixed(1)+' MB'}\n/* the answer as JSON whatever the status: install and certificate errors carry details */\nfunction post(url,body){return fetch(url,body===undefined?{}:{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify(body)})\n  .then(function(r){return r.json().catch(function(){return {error:'The TV answered '+r.status}})})}\nfunction api(url,body){return post(url,body).then(function(d){if(d&&d.error&&d.ok!==true)throw new Error(d.error);return d})}\nfunction base64Of(blob){return new Promise(function(ok,no){var r=new FileReader();r.onload=function(){ok(String(r.result).split(',')[1]||'')};\n  r.onerror=function(){no(new Error('Could not read the file'))};r.readAsDataURL(blob)})}\n\n/* ── the certificate ── */\nvar haveCert=false;\nfunction showCert(c){haveCert=!!(c&&c.author);\n  $('certState').textContent=haveCert?'On the TV: '+(c.author.subject||'author certificate')+(c.author.notAfter?' · valid until '+c.author.notAfter:'')+(c.distributor?'':' · no distributor certificate'):'Not set';\n  $('signNote').textContent=haveCert?'':'add it below first';\n  $('certRemove').hidden=!haveCert;\n  var radios=document.querySelectorAll('input[name=sign]');radios[0].disabled=!haveCert;\n  if(!haveCert)radios[1].checked=true}\nfunction loadCert(first){api('cert').then(function(c){showCert(c);if(first&&haveCert)document.querySelector('input[name=sign][value=sign]').checked=true})\n  .catch(function(e){$('certState').textContent=e.message})}\n$('certSave').onclick=function(){var a=$('authorFile').files[0],d=$('distFile').files[0],b=this;\n  if(!a){$('certStatus').textContent='Choose the author .p12 file.';return}\n  if(a.size>60000||(d&&d.size>60000)){$('certStatus').textContent='That is too large to be a .p12 certificate.';return}\n  b.disabled=true;$('certStatus').textContent='Converting on the TV…';\n  Promise.all([base64Of(a),d?base64Of(d):null]).then(function(f){\n    return api('cert',{author:{p12:f[0],password:$('authorPw').value},distributor:f[1]?{p12:f[1],password:$('distPw').value}:null})})\n  .then(function(c){showCert(c);$('certStatus').textContent='Saved on the TV.';$('authorPw').value='';$('distPw').value='';$('authorFile').value='';$('distFile').value='';\n    document.querySelector('input[name=sign][value=sign]').checked=true})\n  .catch(function(e){$('certStatus').textContent=e.message}).then(function(){b.disabled=false})};\n$('certRemove').onclick=function(){var b=this;if(b.dataset.sure!=='1'){b.dataset.sure='1';b.textContent='Really remove?';b.classList.add('danger');\n    setTimeout(function(){b.dataset.sure='';b.textContent='Remove from the TV';b.classList.remove('danger')},4000);return}\n  api('cert',{remove:true}).then(function(c){showCert(c);$('certStatus').textContent='Removed.'}).catch(function(e){$('certStatus').textContent=e.message})};\n\n/* ── upload and install ── */\nvar picked=null,working=false;\nfunction log(t){var l=$('log');l.hidden=false;l.textContent+=t+String.fromCharCode(10);l.scrollTop=l.scrollHeight}\nfunction pick(f){if(!f)return;var ext=(f.name.split('.').pop()||'').toLowerCase();\n  if(ext!=='wgt'&&ext!=='tpk'){$('status').textContent='Choose a .wgt or .tpk file.';return}\n  picked=f;$('pick').textContent=f.name+' · '+bytes(f.size);$('go').disabled=working;$('status').textContent='Ready to install.'}\n$('file').onchange=function(){pick(this.files&&this.files[0])};\nvar drop=$('drop');\ndrop.ondragover=function(e){e.preventDefault();drop.classList.add('over')};\ndrop.ondragleave=function(){drop.classList.remove('over')};\ndrop.ondrop=function(e){e.preventDefault();drop.classList.remove('over');if(e.dataTransfer&&e.dataTransfer.files.length)pick(e.dataTransfer.files[0])};\n$('go').onclick=function(){if(!picked||working)return;\n  var f=picked,name=f.name.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/g,'_'),size=512*1024,total=Math.max(1,Math.ceil(f.size/size)),n=0;\n  var sign=document.querySelector('input[name=sign]:checked').value==='sign';\n  working=true;$('go').disabled=true;$('log').textContent='';$('progress').hidden=false;$('progress').value=0;\n  log('Uploading '+f.name+' ('+bytes(f.size)+')');\n  function chunk(){return base64Of(f.slice(n*size,Math.min(f.size,(n+1)*size))).then(function(b64){\n      return api('upload',{filename:name,chunk:n,totalChunks:total,data:b64})}).then(function(d){\n      n++;var pct=Math.round(n*100/total);$('progress').value=pct;$('status').textContent='Uploading '+pct+'%';return n<total?chunk():d})}\n  chunk().then(function(d){log('Uploaded. '+(sign?'Signing and installing…':'Installing…'));\n    $('status').textContent=sign?'Signing and installing on the TV…':'Installing on the TV…';\n    return post('install',{file:d.file,sign:sign})})\n  .then(function(r){if(r.output)log(r.output);\n    if(r.ok){var extra=[];if(r.signed)extra.push('signed');if(r.registry&&r.registry.registered)extra.push('added to the app list');\n      if(r.homeRow&&r.homeRow.added)extra.push('tile added to the Home row');\n      log('Installed '+(r.packageId||'')+(extra.length?' · '+extra.join(', '):''));$('status').textContent='Installed '+(r.packageId||f.name)+'.';loadApps()}\n    else{log('Failed'+(r.step==='sign'?' while signing':'')+': '+(r.error||('pkgcmd exit '+r.exit_code)));$('status').textContent='Installation failed. See the log.'}})\n  .catch(function(e){log('Failed: '+e.message);$('status').textContent=e.message})\n  .then(function(){working=false;$('go').disabled=!picked})};\n\n/* ── installed apps ── */\nvar list=[];\nfunction loadApps(){$('apps').innerHTML='<p class=\"note\">Reading the installed apps…</p>';\n  return api('apps').then(function(d){list=d.apps||[];render()}).catch(function(e){$('apps').innerHTML='<p class=\"note\">'+esc(e.message)+'</p>'})}\nfunction render(){var q=$('filter').value.toLowerCase(),sys=$('system').checked;\n  var shown=list.filter(function(a){return (sys||!a.system)&&((a.name+' '+a.packageId+' '+(a.appId||'')).toLowerCase().indexOf(q)>=0)});\n  $('apps').innerHTML=shown.length?shown.map(function(a){return '<div class=\"pkg\"><div><div class=\"pkg-name\">'+esc(a.name)+'<span class=\"tag\">'+esc(a.type)+'</span>'+\n    (a.system?'<span class=\"tag\">system</span>':'')+'</div><div class=\"pkg-id\">'+esc(a.packageId)+(a.version?' · '+esc(a.version):'')+'</div></div><div class=\"row\">'+\n    (a.appId?'<button data-launch=\"'+esc(a.appId)+'\">Launch</button>':'')+\n    (a.system?'':'<button data-home=\"'+esc(a.packageId)+'\">Add to Home</button><button data-uninstall=\"'+esc(a.packageId)+'\">Uninstall</button>')+'</div></div>'}).join('')\n    :'<p class=\"note\">No apps match.</p>'}\n$('filter').oninput=render;$('system').onchange=render;$('refresh').onclick=loadApps;\n$('apps').onclick=function(e){var b=e.target.closest('button');if(!b)return;var d=b.dataset,was=b.textContent;\n  function done(t){b.disabled=false;b.textContent=t;setTimeout(function(){b.textContent=was},3000)}\n  if(d.launch){b.disabled=true;api('launch',{appId:d.launch}).then(function(){done('Launched')}).catch(function(x){done(x.message)})}\n  else if(d.home){b.disabled=true;api('register',{packageId:d.home}).then(function(r){done(r.homeRow&&r.homeRow.added?'Added':'Already there')}).catch(function(x){done(x.message)})}\n  else if(d.uninstall){\n    /* a sandboxed page cannot ask with a dialog: the button asks a second time */\n    if(d.sure!=='1'){d.sure='1';b.textContent='Really uninstall?';b.classList.add('danger');\n      setTimeout(function(){if(b.isConnected&&!b.disabled){d.sure='';b.textContent='Uninstall';b.classList.remove('danger')}},4000);return}\n    b.disabled=true;b.textContent='Uninstalling…';\n    api('uninstall',{packageId:d.uninstall}).then(function(){loadApps()}).catch(function(x){b.disabled=false;d.sure='';b.classList.remove('danger');b.textContent=x.message})}};\n\nloadCert(true);loadApps();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","registry.js":"// Copy of app/service/webapp-registry.js from zabique/vetro (branch extras-050), unchanged below this line: a Shard\n// cannot reach Vetro's own modules, so it carries what it needs.\n'use strict';\n\n// Samsung's web app registry: /opt/dbspace/.webappservice.db, table widgetinfo, kept by org.tizen.webappservice.\n// Samsung Home and the APPS panel only show web apps that have a row there, and the Home drops a row entry\n// whose app has none. Store installs get a row; on some TVs (QN85A, Tizen 6) a sideloaded .wgt installed with\n// pkgcmd never does, not even after a restart of webappservice. register() adds the row the way the store's\n// rows look: a copy of another user-installed web app's row with this app's id, name, paths and app id, plus\n// the icon in the registry's icon folder, then restarts webappservice so it reads the table again.\n\nvar DB = '/opt/dbspace/.webappservice.db';\nvar PKG_DB = '/opt/dbspace/.pkgmgr_parser.db';\nvar ICONS = '/opt/share/webappservice/apps_icon/all/';\nvar BACKUP = '/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vetro-webappservice.db.bak';\nvar ID = /^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}$/;\nvar PATH = /^\\/[A-Za-z0-9_.\\/-]{1,200}$/;\n\nfunction wrap(s) { return 'echo ' + Buffer.from(s).toString('base64') + ' | base64 -d | sh'; }\nfunction check(r) { if (r.exit_code || r.timed_out) throw Error(r.stderr || r.stdout || 'App registry unavailable'); return r.stdout || ''; }\nfunction unhex(v) { return /^(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{2})*$/.test(v || '') ? Buffer.from(v || '', 'hex').toString('utf8') : ''; }\n// Text goes into SQL as a hex blob: no quoting, whatever the app's name holds.\nfunction sqlText(s) { return \"CAST(X'\" + Buffer.from(String(s), 'utf8').toString('hex') + \"' AS TEXT)\"; }\n\nfunction inspectScript(pkg) {\n    return [\n        'echo \"W|$(sqlite3 -readonly ' + DB + ' \"SELECT count(*) FROM widgetinfo WHERE id=\\'' + pkg + '\\';\" 2>/dev/null)\"',\n        'echo \"T|$(sqlite3 -readonly ' + DB + ' \"SELECT id FROM widgetinfo WHERE install_type=\\'user\\' AND pkg_type=\\'wgt\\' AND id!=\\'' + pkg + '\\' ORDER BY app_index LIMIT 1;\" 2>/dev/null)\"',\n        'sqlite3 -readonly ' + PKG_DB + ' \"SELECT \\'A|\\'||hex(a.app_id)||\\'|\\'||a.app_component||\\'|\\'||a.app_nodisplay||\\'|\\'||hex(ifnull(l.app_locale,\\'\\'))||\\'|\\'||hex(ifnull(l.app_label,\\'\\'))||\\'|\\'||hex(ifnull(l.app_icon,\\'\\')) FROM package_app_info a LEFT JOIN package_app_localized_info l ON l.app_id=a.app_id WHERE a.package=\\'' + pkg + '\\';\" 2>/dev/null',\n        'sqlite3 -readonly ' + PKG_DB + ' \"SELECT \\'V|\\'||hex(package_version)||\\'|\\'||package_type FROM package_info WHERE package=\\'' + pkg + '\\';\" 2>/dev/null',\n        'echo \"S|$(du -sk /opt/usr/apps/' + pkg + ' 2>/dev/null | cut -f1)\"',\n        'true'\n    ].join('\\n');\n}\n\n// What the TV knows about a package: {registered, template, version, type, sizeKb, app: {appId, label, icon}}.\nfunction parseInspect(text) {\n    var o = { registered: false, template: null, version: null, type: null, sizeKb: 0, app: null };\n    var apps = {};\n    String(text || '').replace(/\\r/g, '').split('\\n').forEach(function (l) {\n        var f = l.split('|');\n        if (f[0] === 'W') o.registered = Number(f[1]) > 0;\n        else if (f[0] === 'T') o.template = ID.test(f[1] || '') ? f[1] : null;\n        else if (f[0] === 'V') { o.version = unhex(f[1]); o.type = f[2] || null; }\n        else if (f[0] === 'S') o.sizeKb = Number(f[1]) || 0;\n        else if (f[0] === 'A' && f.length >= 7) {\n            var id = unhex(f[1]);\n            if (!ID.test(id) || f[2] !== 'uiapp' || f[3] === 'true') return;   // the visible UI app, not its service\n            var cur = apps[id] || (apps[id] = { appId: id, label: '', icon: '' });\n            var locale = unhex(f[4]);\n            if (!cur.label || locale === 'No Locale') cur.label = unhex(f[5]) || cur.label;\n            if (!cur.icon || locale === 'No Locale') cur.icon = unhex(f[6]) || cur.icon;\n        }\n    });\n    var ids = Object.keys(apps);\n    if (ids.length) o.app = apps[ids[0]];\n    return o;\n}\n\n// Files this agent creates carry its SMACK label (\"User\"), which the Home (User::Pkg::com.samsung.tv.csfs) may not\n// read: it then logs the icon as missing and leaves the tile out. The registry's own icons are labelled \"_\".\nfunction labelScript(pkg) {\n    var dir = ICONS + pkg;\n    return 'if command -v chsmack >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -d ' + dir + ' ]; then chsmack -a _ ' + dir +\n        '; [ -f ' + dir + '/icon.png ] && chsmack -a _ ' + dir + '/icon.png; fi; true';\n}\n\nfunction registerScript(pkg, facts) {\n    var app = facts.app, icon = PATH.test(app.icon || '') ? app.icon : '', dir = ICONS + pkg;\n    var home = '/opt/usr/home/owner/apps_rw/' + pkg + '/';\n    var set = [\n        'id=' + sqlText(pkg), 'title=' + sqlText(app.label || pkg), 'install_path=' + sqlText(home), 'resources_path=' + sqlText(home),\n        'icon_path=' + sqlText(dir + '/'), 'version=' + sqlText(facts.version || '1.0.0'), 'size=' + (facts.sizeKb * 1024),\n        \"install_date=datetime('now','localtime')\", 'tizen_id=' + sqlText(app.appId), 'pkgname=' + sqlText(pkg),\n        'use_count=0', \"launch_date=''\", 'use_gamepad=0', 'is_hidden=0', 'is_display=1',\n        'app_index=(SELECT ifnull(max(app_index),0)+1 FROM widgetinfo)', \"icon_updated_date=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S+00:00','now')\"\n    ].join(', ');\n    var sql = 'BEGIN; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS temp.t; CREATE TEMP TABLE t AS SELECT * FROM widgetinfo WHERE id=\\'' + facts.template + '\\'; UPDATE t SET ' + set +\n        \"; DELETE FROM widgetinfo WHERE id='\" + pkg + \"'; INSERT INTO widgetinfo SELECT * FROM t; COMMIT;\";\n    // The statement sits in double quotes on an sh line: names arrive as hex, so none of these can be in it.\n    if (/[\"$`\\\\]/.test(sql)) throw Error('Unsafe registry statement');\n    return [\n        'set -e',\n        '[ -f ' + BACKUP + ' ] || cp -p ' + DB + ' ' + BACKUP,\n        'mkdir -p ' + dir,\n        icon ? '[ -f \"' + icon + '\" ] && cp \"' + icon + '\" ' + dir + '/icon.png || true' : 'true',\n        'chown -R 5001:users ' + dir + '; chmod 755 ' + dir + '; [ -f ' + dir + '/icon.png ] && chmod 644 ' + dir + '/icon.png || true',\n        labelScript(pkg),\n        'sqlite3 ' + DB + ' \"' + sql + '\"',\n        'chown 5001:users ' + DB + ' ' + DB + '-journal 2>/dev/null || true',\n        'systemctl restart org.tizen.webappservice.service',\n        'sleep 5',\n        'echo \"W|$(sqlite3 -readonly ' + DB + ' \"SELECT count(*) FROM widgetinfo WHERE id=\\'' + pkg + '\\';\")\"'\n    ].join('\\n');\n}\n\n// After an uninstall. webappservice never knew the sideloaded app, so it leaves the row register() made (a ghost\n// tile in Samsung's Apps panel) and the icon folder. Only once the package is really gone; echoes U|<rows removed>.\nfunction unregisterScript(pkg) {\n    var dir = ICONS + pkg;\n    return [\n        'if [ -d /opt/usr/apps/' + pkg + ' ] || [ -n \"$(sqlite3 -readonly ' + PKG_DB + ' \"SELECT 1 FROM package_info WHERE package=\\'' + pkg + '\\';\" 2>/dev/null)\" ]; then echo \"U|installed\"; exit 0; fi',\n        'n=$(sqlite3 -readonly ' + DB + ' \"SELECT count(*) FROM widgetinfo WHERE id=\\'' + pkg + '\\';\" 2>/dev/null)',\n        'if [ \"${n:-0}\" -gt 0 ]; then',\n        '  [ -f ' + BACKUP + ' ] || cp -p ' + DB + ' ' + BACKUP,\n        '  sqlite3 ' + DB + ' \"DELETE FROM widgetinfo WHERE id=\\'' + pkg + '\\';\" || exit 1',\n        '  chown 5001:users ' + DB + ' ' + DB + '-journal 2>/dev/null',\n        '  rm -rf ' + dir,\n        '  systemctl restart org.tizen.webappservice.service',\n        'fi',\n        'echo \"U|${n:-0}\"'\n    ].join('\\n');\n}\n\nfunction Registry(execute) { this.execute = execute; }\n\n// Resolves {removed: rows deleted} or {removed: 0, reason} when the package is still installed.\nRegistry.prototype.unregister = function (pkg) {\n    if (typeof pkg !== 'string' || !ID.test(pkg)) return Promise.reject(Error('Invalid package id'));\n    return this.execute(wrap(unregisterScript(pkg)), 30000).then(function (r) {\n        var m = /U\\|(\\w+)/.exec(check(r));\n        if (!m) throw Error('App registry did not answer');\n        if (m[1] === 'installed') return { removed: 0, reason: pkg + ' is still installed' };\n        return { removed: Number(m[1]) || 0 };\n    });\n};\n\nRegistry.prototype.inspect = function (pkg) {\n    if (typeof pkg !== 'string' || !ID.test(pkg)) return Promise.reject(Error('Invalid package id'));\n    return this.execute(wrap(inspectScript(pkg)), 15000).then(function (r) { return parseInspect(check(r)); });\n};\n\n// Adds the package's web app to the registry unless it has a row. Resolves {registered, added, reason?}.\nRegistry.prototype.register = function (pkg) {\n    var self = this;\n    return this.inspect(pkg).then(function (f) {\n        if (!f.type) throw Error(pkg + ' is not installed');\n        if (f.type !== 'wgt') return { registered: false, added: false, reason: 'Only web apps (.wgt) use this registry' };\n        // Registered already: still give its icon the label the Home can read (rows made before this fix).\n        if (f.registered) return self.execute(wrap(labelScript(pkg)), 10000).then(function () { return { registered: true, added: false }; });\n        if (!f.app) throw Error(pkg + ' has no visible app');\n        if (!f.template) throw Error('No installed web app to model the registry row on');\n        return self.execute(wrap(registerScript(pkg, f)), 40000).then(function (r) {\n            var ok = /W\\|[1-9]/.test(check(r));\n            if (!ok) throw Error('Samsung\\'s app registry did not keep the new row');\n            return { registered: true, added: true, appId: f.app.appId, title: f.app.label };\n        });\n    });\n};\n\nmodule.exports = { Registry: Registry, parseInspect: parseInspect, inspectScript: inspectScript, registerScript: registerScript, labelScript: labelScript, unregisterScript: unregisterScript, sqlText: sqlText, DB: DB };\n","sign.js":"'use strict';\n// Signs a Tizen package (.wgt or .tpk, a zip) in place, the way Tizen Studio does: author-signature.xml and\n// signature1.xml (W3C \"XML Digital Signatures for Widgets\") are added at the top of the archive, older signature\n// files are dropped, every other entry is copied as it is.\n//\n// Only Node's own modules: the archive is read entry by entry (never whole in memory), digests are SHA-512 and\n// the signature is RSA-SHA512 over the canonical SignedInfo. The certificates arrive as PEM material that\n// index.js got from the user's .p12 files with the TV's openssl. Plain ES5.\n\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar zlib = require('zlib');\nvar crypto = require('crypto');\n\nvar DSIG = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#';\nvar SIGNATURE_FILE = /^(author-signature\\.xml|signature[0-9]*\\.xml)$/;\nvar COPY_BLOCK = 1024 * 1024;\n\nfunction buffer(n) { return typeof Buffer.alloc === 'function' ? Buffer.alloc(n) : new Buffer(n).fill(0); }\nfunction fromText(s) { return typeof Buffer.alloc === 'function' ? Buffer.from(s, 'utf8') : new Buffer(s, 'utf8'); }\nfunction wrap76(s) { return s.replace(/(.{76})/g, '$1\\n'); }\nfunction sha512(data) { return crypto.createHash('sha512').update(data).digest('base64'); }\n// A zip path as the URI of a Reference: percent-encoded, then safe inside a double-quoted attribute.\nfunction uriOf(name) { return encodeURI(name).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/\"/g, '&quot;'); }\n\nvar CRC_TABLE = (function () {\n    var t = [], n, k, c;\n    for (n = 0; n < 256; n++) {\n        c = n;\n        for (k = 0; k < 8; k++) c = c & 1 ? 0xEDB88320 ^ (c >>> 1) : c >>> 1;\n        t[n] = c >>> 0;\n    }\n    return t;\n})();\nfunction crc32(buf) {\n    var c = 0xFFFFFFFF;\n    for (var i = 0; i < buf.length; i++) c = CRC_TABLE[(c ^ buf[i]) & 0xFF] ^ (c >>> 8);\n    return (c ^ 0xFFFFFFFF) >>> 0;\n}\n\n// ── the signature document ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// The Object every Tizen signature carries. It is referenced as \"#prop\" through C14N 1.1, where the element\n// stands on its own and so carries the namespace it inherits in the file.\nfunction propObject(id, canonical) {\n    var role = id === 'AuthorSignature' ? 'author' : 'distributor';\n    return '<Object' + (canonical ? ' xmlns=\"' + DSIG + '\"' : '') + ' Id=\"prop\">' +\n        '<SignatureProperties xmlns:dsp=\"http://www.w3.org/2009/xmldsig-properties\">' +\n        '<SignatureProperty Id=\"profile\" Target=\"#' + id + '\">' +\n        '<dsp:Profile URI=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets-digsig#profile\"></dsp:Profile></SignatureProperty>' +\n        '<SignatureProperty Id=\"role\" Target=\"#' + id + '\">' +\n        '<dsp:Role URI=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets-digsig#role-' + role + '\"></dsp:Role></SignatureProperty>' +\n        '<SignatureProperty Id=\"identifier\" Target=\"#' + id + '\">' +\n        '<dsp:Identifier></dsp:Identifier></SignatureProperty></SignatureProperties></Object>';\n}\n\nfunction reference(uri, digest, transform) {\n    return '<Reference URI=\"' + uri + '\">\\n' +\n        (transform ? '<Transforms>\\n<Transform Algorithm=\"http://www.w3.org/2006/12/xml-c14n11\"></Transform>\\n</Transforms>\\n' : '') +\n        '<DigestMethod Algorithm=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#sha512\"></DigestMethod>\\n' +\n        '<DigestValue>' + wrap76(digest) + '</DigestValue>\\n' +\n        '</Reference>\\n';\n}\n\n// id: AuthorSignature or DistributorSignature; refs: [{name, digest}] in archive order;\n// cert: {chain: [base64 DER, leaf first], key: PEM private key}.\nfunction signatureXml(id, refs, cert) {\n    var body = '\\n<CanonicalizationMethod Algorithm=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/xml-exc-c14n#\"></CanonicalizationMethod>\\n' +\n        '<SignatureMethod Algorithm=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmldsig-more#rsa-sha512\"></SignatureMethod>\\n' +\n        refs.map(function (r) { return reference(uriOf(r.name), r.digest, false); }).join('') +\n        reference('#prop', sha512(fromText(propObject(id, true))), true) +\n        '</SignedInfo>';\n    // Exclusive C14N of SignedInfo as written here: the element only gains the namespace it uses.\n    var value = crypto.createSign('RSA-SHA512').update('<SignedInfo xmlns=\"' + DSIG + '\">' + body).sign(cert.key, 'base64');\n    var keyInfo = '<KeyInfo>\\n<X509Data>' + cert.chain.map(function (der) {\n        return '\\n<X509Certificate>\\n' + wrap76(der) + '\\n</X509Certificate>';\n    }).join('') + '\\n</X509Data>\\n</KeyInfo>\\n';\n    return '<Signature xmlns=\"' + DSIG + '\" Id=\"' + id + '\">\\n' +\n        '<SignedInfo>' + body + '\\n' +\n        '<SignatureValue>\\n' + wrap76(value) + '\\n</SignatureValue>\\n' +\n        keyInfo + propObject(id, false) + '\\n</Signature>\\n';\n}\n\n// ── the archive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nfunction readAt(fd, position, length) {\n    var b = buffer(length), got = 0, n;\n    while (got < length) {\n        n = fs.readSync(fd, b, got, length - got, position + got);\n        if (!n) throw new Error('The package is cut short');\n        got += n;\n    }\n    return b;\n}\n\n// The central directory: [{name, raw (its name bytes), flags, method, time, date, crc, csize, usize, offset, ...}].\nfunction readDirectory(fd, size) {\n    if (size < 22) throw new Error('Not a zip archive');\n    var tailLength = Math.min(size, 65557), tail = readAt(fd, size - tailLength, tailLength), at = -1;\n    for (var i = tail.length - 22; i >= 0; i--) if (tail.readUInt32LE(i) === 0x06054b50) { at = i; break; }\n    if (at < 0) throw new Error('Not a zip archive');\n    var count = tail.readUInt16LE(at + 10), dirSize = tail.readUInt32LE(at + 12), dirOffset = tail.readUInt32LE(at + 16);\n    if (count === 0xFFFF || dirOffset === 0xFFFFFFFF || dirOffset + dirSize > size) throw new Error('Zip64 archives are not supported');\n    var dir = readAt(fd, dirOffset, dirSize), p = 0, entries = [];\n    for (var n = 0; n < count; n++) {\n        if (p + 46 > dir.length || dir.readUInt32LE(p) !== 0x02014b50) throw new Error('The zip directory is damaged');\n        var nameLength = dir.readUInt16LE(p + 28), extra = dir.readUInt16LE(p + 30), comment = dir.readUInt16LE(p + 32);\n        var e = {\n            made: dir.readUInt16LE(p + 4), need: dir.readUInt16LE(p + 6), flags: dir.readUInt16LE(p + 8), method: dir.readUInt16LE(p + 10),\n            time: dir.readUInt16LE(p + 12), date: dir.readUInt16LE(p + 14), crc: dir.readUInt32LE(p + 16),\n            csize: dir.readUInt32LE(p + 20), usize: dir.readUInt32LE(p + 24), internal: dir.readUInt16LE(p + 36),\n            external: dir.readUInt32LE(p + 38), offset: dir.readUInt32LE(p + 42), raw: dir.slice(p + 46, p + 46 + nameLength)\n        };\n        e.name = e.raw.toString('utf8');\n        if (e.flags & 1) throw new Error('Encrypted archives are not supported');\n        if (e.csize === 0xFFFFFFFF || e.usize === 0xFFFFFFFF || e.offset === 0xFFFFFFFF) throw new Error('Zip64 archives are not supported');\n        if (e.method !== 0 && e.method !== 8) throw new Error('Unsupported compression in ' + e.name);\n        entries.push(e);\n        p += 46 + nameLength + extra + comment;\n    }\n    return entries;\n}\n\n// Where an entry's bytes start: after its local header, whose name and extra lengths are its own.\nfunction dataStart(fd, e) {\n    var h = readAt(fd, e.offset, 30);\n    if (h.readUInt32LE(0) !== 0x04034b50) throw new Error('The zip is damaged at ' + e.name);\n    return e.offset + 30 + h.readUInt16LE(26) + h.readUInt16LE(28);\n}\n\n// The digest of one entry's content, without blocking the service while a big file inflates.\nfunction digestOf(fd, e, done) {\n    var raw;\n    try { raw = readAt(fd, dataStart(fd, e), e.csize); } catch (x) { return done(x); }\n    if (e.method === 0) return setImmediate(function () { done(null, sha512(raw)); });\n    zlib.inflateRaw(raw, function (err, data) {\n        if (err) return done(new Error('Could not read ' + e.name + ' from the package'));\n        done(null, sha512(data));\n    });\n}\n\nfunction dosTime(d) {\n    return { time: (d.getHours() << 11) | (d.getMinutes() << 5) | (d.getSeconds() >> 1),\n        date: (Math.max(0, d.getFullYear() - 1980) << 9) | ((d.getMonth() + 1) << 5) | d.getDate() };\n}\n\nfunction localHeader(e) {\n    var h = buffer(30);\n    h.writeUInt32LE(0x04034b50, 0); h.writeUInt16LE(e.need, 4); h.writeUInt16LE(e.flags & ~8, 6); h.writeUInt16LE(e.method, 8);\n    h.writeUInt16LE(e.time, 10); h.writeUInt16LE(e.date, 12); h.writeUInt32LE(e.crc, 14); h.writeUInt32LE(e.csize, 18);\n    h.writeUInt32LE(e.usize, 22); h.writeUInt16LE(e.raw.length, 26); h.writeUInt16LE(0, 28);\n    return Buffer.concat([h, e.raw]);\n}\nfunction directoryRecord(e, offset) {\n    var h = buffer(46);\n    h.writeUInt32LE(0x02014b50, 0); h.writeUInt16LE(e.made, 4); h.writeUInt16LE(e.need, 6); h.writeUInt16LE(e.flags & ~8, 8);\n    h.writeUInt16LE(e.method, 10); h.writeUInt16LE(e.time, 12); h.writeUInt16LE(e.date, 14); h.writeUInt32LE(e.crc, 16);\n    h.writeUInt32LE(e.csize, 20); h.writeUInt32LE(e.usize, 24); h.writeUInt16LE(e.raw.length, 28);\n    h.writeUInt16LE(e.internal, 36); h.writeUInt32LE(e.external, 38); h.writeUInt32LE(offset, 42);\n    return Buffer.concat([h, e.raw]);\n}\n\n// A new entry made here (a signature file).\nfunction newEntry(name, text, when) {\n    var data = fromText(text), packed = zlib.deflateRawSync(data), t = dosTime(when);\n    return { made: 20, need: 20, flags: 0x0800, method: 8, time: t.time, date: t.date, crc: crc32(data), csize: packed.length,\n        usize: data.length, internal: 0, external: 0, raw: fromText(name), name: name, packed: packed };\n}\n\n// file: the package, rewritten in place. certs: {author: {chain, key}, distributor?: {chain, key}}.\n// Resolves {files: entries signed, size: bytes of the signed package, distributor: true|false}.\nfunction signPackage(file, certs, now) {\n    return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n        var fd = null, out = null, temp = file + '.signing';\n        function fail(e) {\n            try { if (fd !== null) fs.closeSync(fd); } catch (x) { /* closing */ }\n            try { if (out !== null) fs.closeSync(out); } catch (x) { /* closing */ }\n            try { fs.unlinkSync(temp); } catch (x) { /* never made */ }\n            reject(e);\n        }\n        try {\n            if (!certs || !certs.author || !certs.author.key || !certs.author.chain || !certs.author.chain.length) throw new Error('No author certificate');\n            fd = fs.openSync(file, 'r');\n            var entries = readDirectory(fd, fs.fstatSync(fd).size).filter(function (e) { return !SIGNATURE_FILE.test(e.name); });\n            var files = entries.filter(function (e) { return !/\\/$/.test(e.name); });\n            if (!files.length) throw new Error('The package holds no files');\n        } catch (e) { return fail(e); }\n\n        var index = 0;\n        (function next() {\n            if (index === files.length) return write();\n            var e = files[index++];\n            digestOf(fd, e, function (err, digest) {\n                if (err) return fail(err);\n                e.digest = digest;\n                next();\n            });\n        })();\n\n        function write() {\n            try {\n                var when = now || new Date();\n                var refs = files.map(function (e) { return { name: e.name, digest: e.digest }; });\n                var authorXml = signatureXml('AuthorSignature', refs, certs.author);\n                var added = [newEntry('author-signature.xml', authorXml, when)];\n                if (certs.distributor) {\n                    var all = [{ name: 'author-signature.xml', digest: sha512(fromText(authorXml)) }].concat(refs);\n                    added.push(newEntry('signature1.xml', signatureXml('DistributorSignature', all, certs.distributor), when));\n                }\n                out = fs.openSync(temp, 'w');\n                var position = 0, records = [];\n                added.forEach(function (e) {\n                    records.push(directoryRecord(e, position));\n                    var head = localHeader(e);\n                    fs.writeSync(out, head, 0, head.length); fs.writeSync(out, e.packed, 0, e.packed.length);\n                    position += head.length + e.packed.length;\n                });\n                var i = 0;\n                (function copy() {\n                    try {\n                        if (i === entries.length) return finish(position, records, added.length + entries.length);\n                        var e = entries[i++], from = dataStart(fd, e), left = e.csize, head = localHeader(e);\n                        records.push(directoryRecord(e, position));\n                        fs.writeSync(out, head, 0, head.length);\n                        position += head.length + e.csize;\n                        while (left > 0) {\n                            var block = readAt(fd, from, Math.min(left, COPY_BLOCK));\n                            fs.writeSync(out, block, 0, block.length);\n                            from += block.length; left -= block.length;\n                        }\n                        setImmediate(copy);     // one entry per turn: the service keeps answering\n                    } catch (e2) { fail(e2); }\n                })();\n            } catch (e) { fail(e); }\n        }\n\n        function finish(position, records, count) {\n            try {\n                var dir = Buffer.concat(records), end = buffer(22);\n                if (count > 0xFFFE || position + dir.length > 0xFFFFFFFE) throw new Error('The package is too large to sign');\n                end.writeUInt32LE(0x06054b50, 0); end.writeUInt16LE(count, 8); end.writeUInt16LE(count, 10);\n                end.writeUInt32LE(dir.length, 12); end.writeUInt32LE(position, 16);\n                fs.writeSync(out, dir, 0, dir.length); fs.writeSync(out, end, 0, end.length);\n                fs.closeSync(out); out = null;\n                fs.closeSync(fd); fd = null;\n                fs.renameSync(temp, file);\n                resolve({ files: files.length, size: position + dir.length + 22, distributor: !!certs.distributor });\n            } catch (e) { fail(e); }\n        }\n    });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { signPackage: signPackage, signatureXml: signatureXml, readDirectory: readDirectory, crc32: crc32, propObject: propObject };\n"}}
